  "source_description": "SENSEX entry model, label=0.10% (5min horizon), trained 2026-09-12 as part of the multi-instrument feature-ceiling investigation: 70 features (47 baseline + 20 verified opening-range/chain/ladder additions + atm_ce_iv/atm_pe_iv/price_vs_vwap -- SENSEX is one of only 2 instruments with 100% price_vs_vwap coverage, its full history starts 2026-01-01), train ..2026-06-01, valid 2026-06-02..07-15, holdout 2026-07-16..08-06. Deployed at threshold 0.50, default exit policy (its own sweep confirmed the default EXIT_MAX_LOSS_PCT=0.10 already sits at the optimal plateau, no retuning needed). Real canonical backtest (2026-07-16..08-06, SENSEX's own holdout window -- its full history ends 2026-08-06 with no post-holdout room, unlike the other instruments): 8 live trades, 75% win, PF=3.06, +4.02% return. REOPENED 2026-09-12 after the prior 'closed negative' verdict for this instrument could not be reproduced and was found to be wrong (root cause not identified, source script no longer existed) -- see project_sensex_entry_system_status memory for the full reproduction investigation. NOT certified bug-free, and unlike BankNifty/NIFTY this candidate has NOT had direction-forensics review. Deployed PAPER-ONLY -- an operator_halt file was added specifically for this deployment (SENSEX did not have one before; its buyer path had genuine real-execution capability, confirmed via recent tier=live trades as recently as 2026-09-10) so this rollout does not change real trading behavior, only paper telemetry.",
